## High-Signal Events

Not all messages are equal. Some are worth analyzing immediately rather than waiting for the buffer to fill:

```typescript
private isHighSignal(entry: ReviewEntry): boolean {
  // Blocked by CoherenceGate = the LLM reviewers found something
  if (entry.result.blockedBy === 'coherence-gate') return true;

  // Multiple warnings = pattern emerging
  if ((entry.result.warnings?.length ?? 0) >= 3) return true;

  // Convergence block = heuristic pattern match
  if (entry.result.blockedBy === 'convergence') return true;

  return false;
}
```

Blocked messages are the richest signal. They represent moments where the agent's natural output was *wrong enough to catch*. The ConvergenceChecker's 7 categories (settling, fabrication, sycophancy, etc.) are already taxonomized — when they fire, the LearningExtractor knows exactly what kind of pattern to look for.

---

## Batch Summary Construction

The LLM doesn't need full message text for every entry. Build a token-efficient summary:

```typescript
private buildBatchSummary(batch: ReviewEntry[]): string {
  return batch.map((entry, i) => {
    const status = entry.result.pass ? 'PASSED' : `BLOCKED (${entry.result.blockedBy})`;
    const warnings = entry.result.warnings?.length
      ? `\nWarnings: ${entry.result.warnings.join(', ')}`
      : '';

    // Truncate long messages to save tokens
    const msgPreview = entry.request.message.length > 500
      ? entry.request.message.slice(0, 500) + '... [truncated]'
      : entry.request.message;

    return `### Message ${i + 1} [${entry.request.channelId}] — ${status}${warnings}\n${msgPreview}`;
  }).join('\n\n');
}
```

